# Thread 10 — 💡 SUGGESTION: `normalizeFinding` synthesizes a note from `reason`

**Fixed as proposed.** In `js/common/tcMaintenanceLedger.js`, `FINDING_FIELD_TABLE`'s `note` entry no longer falls back to `reason` — `findingField('note', src)` now reads only an explicit `note`. The non-loose fields keep their fallbacks (`reason` ← `comment`, `evidence` ← `diff`). Effect:

- automation findings (`findingFromVerdict` / `findingFromDevClaim`) get `note: null` from `firstDefined(['note'])` and carry their detail in `reason` exactly as before — so the same text is **not** duplicated across the digest columns;
- human-entered ledger lines that carry an explicit `note` (the documented extension path) are still preserved verbatim;
- a dev claim with both `note` and `reason` keeps them separate in the digest; with only `reason`, the note column stays empty.

Tests updated/added in `js/unit-tests/test_tcMaintenanceLedger.js`: a finding with `note + reason` renders both; a finding with only `reason` no longer mirrors it into the note column; `normalizeFinding` round-trips a human-supplied note. The CLI `--note` flag path (which sets `note` explicitly) is unchanged by construction.

